/ The month is chosen on the registration site, behind the same link as the
/ subscription. A button of its own would lead to the very same place, so this
/ stays a sentence. It shares the line with the button, because it qualifies
/ what the button leads to.
/
/ It is rendered in both branches of the page: whoever cannot start the month
/ can still tell the person who can, and their button is the login.
/
/ The distance to what comes before belongs to the caller, which is what puts
/ this on a line or on its own.
/
/ No color and no line of its own. The sentence is an offer and not a warning,
/ and next to the button it is read without one. The only mark it carries is
/ the word the offer stands on, which the text sets in strong.
- if PremiumStatus.trial_available?
  p
    == t('sponsoring.show.trial')
